    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0674" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    CFM Files: Lot M–88: Box 121: File—Occupation
                    Statute, Cables: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Military Governor for Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Clay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of the Army
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-18">December 18, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CC–7108. To Dept of Army for CSCAD from CINCEUR signed Clay. The 6th meeting of the French, US, and UK Military
                    Governors took place in Frankfurt on 16 Dec 1948.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d390-f1"
                    /> It was a long 9 hour meeting interrupted in the middle by a conference with
                    representatives from the Parliamentary Assembly concerning which I will advise
                    you by separate cable.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d390-f2"/> The formal agenda was as
                    follows:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">1. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft Occupation Statute</hi>
                </p>
                <p>“In discussion of the current draft at this meeting it was very apparent that
                    instead of it being possible for us to reduce our minor disagreements it seemed
                    that we were introducing new points of interpretation upon which we did not
                    completely agree. We therefore <pb facs="0675" n="641" xml:id="pg641"/> ceased
                    discussion of the Occupation Statute and agreed to refer it to our governments
                    in its present form for resolution of the outstanding differences. However, we
                    did agree on a formal report to our governments delineating the outstanding
                    disagreements and asking for a reconciliation of these disagreements.” This
                    document has been cabled separately.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d390-f3"/> The present
                    draft Occupation Statute is being dispatched to you by courier.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d390-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>[The remainder of this message reported on the discussion of the trade agreement
                    between France and Western Germany, the Military Security Board, the Ruhr,
                    prohibited and limited industries, and civil aviation in Western Germany. For
                    portions of this message dealing with the Ruhr, see <ref target="#pg572">page
                        572</ref>. For Ambassador Murphy’s
                    notes of the portion of this meeting devoted to the Military Security Board, see
                        <ref target="#pg667">page 667</ref>. For documentation regarding the
                    question of limited and prohibited industries, see <ref target="#pg668">pages
                        668</ref> ff.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Clay</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d390-f1" n="1" xml:id="d390-f1-content">
                <p>The American Delegation minutes of this two-part meeting, documents TRIB/USDel/M(48) 2 and 3, December 22 and December 16,
                    respectively, are included in the CFM Files, Lot
                    M–88, Box 121, File—Occupation Statute.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d390-f2" n="2" xml:id="d390-f2-content">
                <p>The cable under reference is not printed, but see Minutes of the meeting between
                    the Military Governors and the Parliamentary Council Delegation, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d390-f3" n="3" xml:id="d390-f3-content">
                <p>General Clay’s cable (7107) is not
                    printed; the Report of the Military Governors is printed, <ref target="#pg650"
                        >p. 650</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d390-f4" n="4" xml:id="d390-f4-content">
                <p>The Draft Joint Text of the Occupation Statute (Appendix “B” to TRIB/P(48)14/1–TOS/P(48)1/6)
                    is printed, <ref target="#pg653">p. 653</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
